   "source": [
    "### [2] Point Geometry"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c70f4784-31d7-44c8-90b6-3cfe2af646cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "the basics of any graphing, is that each point has a coordinate for x and y."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6a24e4f5-1ee1-4692-8b13-818fa7ba8ec4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "a fairly advanced example of this is seen below - however the core of ggplot remains the same (as above)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "f17be84c-6eaf-4771-8ecc-0103aed9f1cc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#basics of any graph - each point has a coordinate for x and y\n",
    "\n",
    "scat2 <- ggplot(data=college) +\n",
    "  geom_point(mapping=aes(x=tuition, y=sat_avg,shape=control),colour='purple')+#shape can be used if you have factor variables\n",
    "   labs(title = \"Tuition has still not gone out of style\",\n",
    "         subtitle = \"Fairly strong positive correlation remains between tuition hours received and SAT Scores\",\n",
    "         caption = \"Standardised, collected by the board for economic opportunity\",\n",
    "         tag = \"Fig. 1\")+\n",
    "  theme(plot.caption = element_text(hjust=0.5,color='purple4'),\n",
    "        plot.title = element_text(colour='purple4',size=20,face='bold'),\n",
    "        plot.subtitle= element_text(colour='purple3',size=13,face='bold'))+\n",
    "  theme(panel.background=element_rect(fill='#fff9fc',linetype=4,linewidth=1,colour='purple4'),\n",
    "        plot.background=element_rect(fill = '#f1e7ff',linewidth=1,colour='purple4'))"
   ]
  },
