  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c04b1168-ca31-4e19-b53d-6f179b94a414",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Quick recap on group_by() and R's answer to pivot tables:**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 51,
   "id": "0f7212b6-e16d-4813-b387-3b73b3fa918b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#?group_by() #this is effectively saying =SUMIF() and forming a new table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "d57c27dc-912d-428d-9516-bc76763d51f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# instead of...\n",
    "# Name    | Region | Sales \n",
    "# Mary    | North  | 30\n",
    "# Phil    | North  | 30\n",
    "# Cara    | South  | 70\n",
    "# Elliot  | North  | 15\n",
    "# William | South  | 12\n",
    "# Emma    | South  | 50"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "1776f19f-7528-4775-b3bc-b1ad71b55a77",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# test <- dataframe %>%\n",
    "#   group_by(Region) %>%\n",
    "#   summarise(Total=sum(Sales))\n",
    "# \n",
    "# we get\n",
    "# \n",
    "# Region | TotalSales \n",
    "# North  | 30+30+15 = 75\n",
    "# South  | 70+12+50 = 132"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aa4f186b-ea03-45e2-879c-2e5352f9ae64",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "(be warned its just grouping, e.g. for max/min searches through all the north/south values)<br>\n",
    "so in effect; group_by() groups the table so R treats them the same (adding to the \"column\" field; then the summarise() makes the table completely) "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "id": "0d45a642-6893-4401-acba-5c9e1b22733a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "m <- \"adding another column to the group(by) simply does that; add another column\"\n",
    "# test <- dataframe %>%\n",
    "#   group_by(Region,Season) %>%\n",
    "#   summarise(Total=sum(Sales),.groups=\"drop\") -> R; its ok to stop grouping now\n",
    "#   "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c4905067-bdef-40ad-8495-f57107a28ab5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If u wanted to combine and have one of the variables be wide; just separately do a pivot_wider() operation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "5a8d6752-514e-49d1-8ddb-dd9d959d7bde",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# pivot_wider(dataframe,names_from=Season, values_from=Total)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5135956b-0e86-43f6-9613-e2d27e25a8f4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Doing this means the original total column has been spread effectively into the four seasons<br>Hence you have to make a new column for total just do mutate(dataframe,Total=spring+summer+autumn+winter)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "55bfee24-daac-4926-8486-2a714421fbbf",
   "metadata": {
    "jp-MarkdownHeadingCollapsed": true
   },
