   "source": [
    "### [9] Using scale_ functions in ggplot"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4c602fdf-78ce-4056-a321-c44067d8fe00",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**'Scales describe how data is mapped from the dataset to the visualisation.'<br>\n",
    "'Both discreet and continous scales exist; for discreet and continous variables respectively'**\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0241d910-d267-4f38-a34a-b8adb18710d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "To map a scale, follow the format scale_name_datatype:<br>\n",
    "> *scale_y_discrete* | discrete variable on the y axis<br>\n",
    "> *scale_x_continous* | continous variable on the x axis<br>\n",
    "> *scale_fill_discrete* | discrete variable on the 'fill' axis/scale"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a28ec3f4-70d3-43db-ad0c-35b1f7facb20",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Using Plot4 again; we can change label names using scale_"
